/commit/6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125","sha":"6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125"}],"sha":"6a00291a266c9e581523de24d56ac2ecda6462d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/6a00291a266c9e581523de24d56ac2ecda6462d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25431636?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alb3rtino","id":25431636,"login":"alb3rtino","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NDMxNjM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T09:15:18Z","email":"alb3rtino@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alb3rtino"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T09:15:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STRWEB-158 Exclude consumer test files from type checking (#189)\n\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STRWEB-158\n\n## Purpose\n\n`webpack/tsconfig.json` extends `include` four levels up\n(`../../../../src/**/*.ts(x)`) to cover a consuming project''s source\ntree, but `exclude` is not extended to the same depth. As a result,\nconsumer test files under `src/` (e.g.\n`src/components/Foo/Foo.test.tsx`) are pulled into the type-check\nprogram created by `fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin`. A type-only issue\nin such a file blocks `stripes build`, even though the consumer''s own\n`tsc` may pass. Test files are not part of the production bundle, so\nincluding them in the build''s type-check program adds little value while\ncreating friction. Excluding them keeps responsibilities cleanly\nseparated between `stripes build` and the consumer''s own `tsc --noEmit`\n/ `yarn test`.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `../../../../src/**/*.test.ts` and `../../../../src/**/*.test.tsx`\nto the `exclude` list in `webpack/tsconfig.json` to match the depth of\nthe existing `include` patterns.","tree":{"sha":"c9e6a4349a375cfce02d6ccf1063373d19d205d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/git/trees/c9e6a4349a375cfce02d6ccf1063373d19d205d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/git/commits/6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125","verification":{"payload":"tree c9e6a4349a375cfce02d6ccf1063373d19d205d8\nparent 512a0d2840d56c1df32eca073c00cc2430c7e86e\nauthor alb3rtino <alb3rtino@users.noreply.github.com> 1778318118 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778318118 +0200\n\nSTRWEB-158 Exclude consumer test files from type checking (#189)\n\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STRWEB-158\n\n## Purpose\n\n`webpack/tsconfig.json` extends `include` four levels up\n(`../../../../src/**/*.ts(x)`) to cover a consuming project''s source\ntree, but `exclude` is not extended to the same depth. As a result,\nconsumer test files under `src/` (e.g.\n`src/components/Foo/Foo.test.tsx`) are pulled into the type-check\nprogram created by `fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin`. A type-only issue\nin such a file blocks `stripes build`, even though the consumer''s own\n`tsc` may pass. Test files are not part of the production bundle, so\nincluding them in the build''s type-check program adds little value while\ncreating friction. Excluding them keeps responsibilities cleanly\nseparated between `stripes build` and the consumer''s own `tsc --noEmit`\n/ `yarn test`.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `../../../../src/**/*.test.ts` and `../../../../src/**/*.test.tsx`\nto the `exclude` list in `webpack/tsconfig.json` to match the depth of\nthe existing `include` patterns.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/vsmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAvMQADDAlZF10N2lphxGH/CBE+Ct\nLbPPmS+ph03ukztSbaMITaO+qrIA5vaEOLrcQYZiiw71XSoKna6CyOGxUS8g5e0h\n8pyKH2uNMoSPLm4s2k6uD4VBdNCE5Fs5qEeOdOMnbRk2oVYUbkLLv4klrIGj5rDf\nciU55cTJcKER90yUexp0g8S9PRwUhc+u6xUIW7Pp8MRFLtJqxmFHveHwwd4Kabu1\nZkpx0yTuBsuriWmOa4IfqfmLKAsA4g0s/8dcBVjCv19p3NP+kHkMwnIC0qEI9UcR\niq9KWaIx38XbnGgq3yCRWJtRrnfw88aHcOfqFz+d7C/fARHZLxeaiSzftesSVG7X\n1p/nfke814Y490vExQV3gFnnDQoyN8jVaSGngSnF8GHQAaW0srSE+qjvbMphGzFG\n4Iod8wgbZVxYgThDffJ9hN6OpV9PLsIj6bBXGihPbXCRBualpH0P1GzmBTynLWgr\nP9/SjDAYupCTsSB8zTJnt8hR/F4tnluEhm+9WD5oCafrnExMFD/2fx2A7s+UHob1\nJJQBnrCS7XL6ldLvBeabyaH4UpXstwuOimvwVNwnrO1NsAJNXPmnUZW+nRTfUUHf\njUbPQGGkCebIOVTFIXrQG/rU5MyucNCEHZM6plcGEk9LIZ4pPoueAhfKqQyysr6S\nmQcwJ+oMCGdjmzS/CjE+\n=KZJ9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T09:15:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commit/6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125","node_id":"C_kwDOE9ZCXNoAKDZjZDAwZGY2ZmY4YzMzNjU2YjdiZTllYzE0NTQzZjQwMTBiNDExMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commit/512a0d2840d56c1df32eca073c00cc2430c7e86e","sha":"512a0d2840d56c1df32eca073c00cc2430c7e86e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/512a0d2840d56c1df32eca073c00cc2430c7e86e"}],"sha":"6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/6cd00df6ff8c33656b7be9ec14543f4010b41125"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25431636?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alb3rtino","id":25431636,"login":"alb3rtino","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NDMxNjM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alb3rtino","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/512a0d2840d56c1df32eca073c00cc2430c7e86e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T19:49:43Z","email":"alb3rtino@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alb3rtino"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T19:49:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STRWEB-156 Gracefully handle a missing favicon (#188)\n\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STRWEB-156\n\n## Purpose\n\nRunning `yarn start` (i.e. `stripes serve`) in a module repository\nwithout a `stripes.config.js` fails during webpack configuration. The\ndefault config does not define `branding.favicon.src`, and the fallback\n`FAVICON_PATH` is resolved relative to the current working directory,\nwhere the asset typically does not exist. As a result, developers have\nto manually create a `stripes.config.js` or place a favicon at\n`./tenant-assets/folio-favicon.png` to start a module locally.\n\n#184 worked around this for the test environment by suppressing the\nmissing-favicon error when `NODE_ENV === ''test''`, but the underlying\nissue remains for `yarn start`. This PR removes that special case and\nresolves the favicon uniformly across environments.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduced `resolveFaviconPath` helper that returns the configured\nfavicon if it exists, the default `FAVICON_PATH` if it exists, or the\nbundled `default-assets/favicon.svg` otherwise.\n- A configured `branding.favicon.src` that does not exist still throws,\nso a typo in a tenant config remains a hard error.\n- Removed the now unused `isTesting` flag.\n- Updated `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","tree":{"sha":"60fe461f7fe418285c5e70d5a9cb6083ec5c95bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/git/trees/60fe461f7fe418285c5e70d5a9cb6083ec5c95bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/git/commits/512a0d2840d56c1df32eca073c00cc2430c7e86e","verification":{"payload":"tree 60fe461f7fe418285c5e70d5a9cb6083ec5c95bb\nparent 7a3e84a531aefb13c8acc1c0b672e1366854f31c\nauthor alb3rtino <alb3rtino@users.noreply.github.com> 1778183383 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778183383 +0200\n\nSTRWEB-156 Gracefully handle a missing favicon (#188)\n\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STRWEB-156\n\n## Purpose\n\nRunning `yarn start` (i.e. `stripes serve`) in a module repository\nwithout a `stripes.config.js` fails during webpack configuration. The\ndefault config does not define `branding.favicon.src`, and the fallback\n`FAVICON_PATH` is resolved relative to the current working directory,\nwhere the asset typically does not exist. As a result, developers have\nto manually create a `stripes.config.js` or place a favicon at\n`./tenant-assets/folio-favicon.png` to start a module locally.\n\n#184 worked around this for the test environment by suppressing the\nmissing-favicon error when `NODE_ENV === ''test''`, but the underlying\nissue remains for `yarn start`. This PR removes that special case and\nresolves the favicon uniformly across environments.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduced `resolveFaviconPath` helper that returns the configured\nfavicon if it exists, the default `FAVICON_PATH` if it exists, or the\nbundled `default-assets/favicon.svg` otherwise.\n- A configured `branding.favicon.src` that does not exist still throws,\nso a typo in a tenant config remains a hard error.\n- Removed the now unused `isTesting` flag.\n- Updated `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/OzXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg5sQAF6QLgtZt5tRjIvKmP3TmYpp\n6jHBVVjSpbqAtdSuHlOasncDKR3bopvwho/fqJVrQEEpN36pFKPcGDmMsm6gl9V4\nQ+0irBbRsfMS0GaUBuMZ6zLR0f+kARwJreQ47p5wGWOyDYxQ2z4ktqoJEoBspeUv\nejqMeaiJW5+3rTg6KEf3Q4uEcWI/FauQCx+RMTSvTfAPfce/b/qepXFwVzQw++5D\nCndlfO5W7LBJMW1HpXIrGxgDqGHxGhANCKLGVHaUsYn8yIahk4kVwYNyOQIqSN9O\n00qffkkQt/f3L9ar9jYSzYxtbSwhttRUNrR1CLawi+DdyllMVeLc38tGvhXvnYlD\ngj0C4WDmFmwYf5bIZ5riI6Ij7XU2MCnuHP+IoSkrRfJY+xMwdmoxSku8Pa5tWDi2\nuN8P++7w96xvNmhc1pJ2MPXxSvrZe2Y+ZNn/YSaiTZR881dWQZcmPnJTnJSySZr