/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/commits/cd4c1b9866931a47f3b47bc3e5db09a9fdfc6a1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-06T20:30:44Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-06T20:30:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STRWEB-151 use the given favicon without favicons-webpack-plugin (#179)\n\nRather than processing the file given in `stripes.config.js`\n`branding.favicon.src` through `favicons-webpack-plugin`, supply it directly\nto webpack''s built-in `html-webpack-plugin` handler. Without the\npost-processing provided by `favicons-webpack-plugin`, this means we rely\non the sysop who builds a bundle to provide sensible data. Previously, a\n10MB jpg would be resized and reformatted to something sensible for use\nas a browser-tab icon but now that file will be used as-is.\n\nThe primary motivating factor here is that `favicons-webpack-plugin`\nrequires `sharp`, a utility that is installed via an insecure post-install\nscript. A secondary factor is that browser support for favicons has\nchanged substantially since this work was done, allowing us to reduce\nthe number of required images.\n\nRefs STRWEB-151","tree":{"sha":"fbd55fbae6adeb5aa15096d5ae4258867c519741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/git/trees/fbd55fbae6adeb5aa15096d5ae4258867c519741"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-webpack/git/commits/cd4c1b9866931a47f3b47bc3e5db09a9fdfc6a1d","verification":{"payload":"tree fbd55fbae6adeb5aa15096d5ae4258867c519741\nparent caf5aff321efa0f143e80372d510f2584a3da951\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1775507444 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775507444 -0400\n\nSTRWEB-151 use the given favicon without favicons-webpack-plugin (#179)\n\nRather than processing the file given in `stripes.config.js`\n`branding.favicon.src` through `favicons-webpack-plugin`, supply it directly\nto webpack''s built-in `html-webpack-plugin` handler. Without the\npost-processing provided by `favicons-webpack-plugin`, this means we rely\non the sysop who builds a bundle to provide sensible data. Previously, a\n10MB jpg would be resized and reformatted to something sensible for use\nas a browser-tab icon but now that file will be used as-is.\n\nThe primary motivating factor here is that `favicons-webpack-plugin`\nrequires `sharp`, a utility that is installed via an insecure post-install\nscript. A secondary factor is that browser support for favicons has\nchanged substantially since this work was done, allowing us to reduce\nthe number of required images.\n\nRefs STRWEB-151","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp1Bf0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADBoQAEXou04Y1raVvPVeFGZcioSi\nbFA76OkbAMrE/0TtiBQsg8YdhUtibwxoHtEDv5UW62H4f56sc93Dkxt9mSWDBY7E\nmACRk1dgQLkmi6AZDy0j3Zbp6nq+exZm+iu8uLVIaF8TojIODKMSMayNhSpngSu0\nHchLSSMZHABoMzOYVTr0ehpaJlrlq9gKefP/8Za77fgj3mGhA9dFUkbn+M1Zn/zS\nCTZ4hs2p2aLerSwQ34pYLPzxcIfUmrN2WIi5fWUNQ50AjT/lbLeZdK6KWzJ2F3un\nMOzYRtN8T2XG2li6IdmRUCK66wUgrm6TsOZqWHAaFY+9olk88lVweSQUzsvMvf5/\nOwtTkpJd19X3UEhrHaOx0jsxKKgBq7N5tbxW1QZxTW7cMDyLaK6aybUhRNa/Jzjs\nmriXMsweWqd5Iy2WQftxzGjfiMKi9XSVv3ogVN6pW7Kol3IzZxnRdyHej+UEc6eX\ni