rification\n\n- fix allowed_hosts with Postgres: pgx resolves the hostname itself and dials the resolved IPs,\n  so the hostname is now verified at lookup time (LookupHost) and each IP at dial time (DialResolvedContext)\n- refuse URLs containing credentials (userinfo)\n- drop the Content-Location header (in addition to Location) pointing to another origin, whatever the status code\n- the most specific network wins between allowed and denied networks, so allowing a large network\n  doesn''t re-allow the Kubernetes API service IP or the cloud metadata endpoints\n- deny direct requests to the address of the HTTP proxy configured in the environment,\n  as the connections to the proxy are not verified\n- verify the OAuth token URL when saving a (global) secret and before requesting a token\n- verify the local datasources of the ephemeral dashboards\n- deny more cloud metadata / credentials endpoints (AWS ECS, EKS Pod Identity, Azure WireServer, Oracle legacy)\n- compare the scheme, host and effective port when checking the origin of a location\n- share a single guard (ServiceManager.GetProxyGuard) and require it to be non-nil\n- avoid extracting the proxy config twice when building a proxy\n- clarify the startup warning when ''security.enable_auth'' is false\n- split the proxy implementation in http.go and sql.go\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [DOC] document the datasource proxy breaking changes and add configuration examples\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] merge back the HTTP and SQL proxies in proxy.go to ease the review, the split will be done in a dedicated PR\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [BUGFIX] address the review of the datasource proxy destination verification\n\n- refuse the IPv4 addresses in a non-canonical notation (e.g. 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 127.1),\n  not resolved by the Go resolver but translated by most HTTP proxies (WHATWG \"ends in a number\" rule)\n- deny the HTTP proxy of the environment as a destination through the proxy itself, not only directly\n- log at debug level when a destination cannot be resolved before being sent to the HTTP proxy\n- report a connection to the OAuth token URL denied at connection time as a 403,\n  as golang.org/x/oauth2 doesn''t wrap the error of the HTTP client\n- verify the proxy destination in /api/validate/datasources and /api/validate/globaldatasources\n- log the denied destinations and the dropped location headers at debug level for the unsaved datasources\n- define the supported URL schemes in the config package (config.SchemeHTTP, config.SchemeHTTPS)\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] fix the merge of main: restore deniedDestinationMsg and align the proxy tests with secureResponse\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] document why deniedErrorRecorder is needed\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkc8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsJwQAFBA6K6t/W/nJ2Zw35G8c65L\n05N/2hjOW4WR4JFteloMv2jdWsh159Qgl2npOGwtZMxeTAdC/CEeX4tcFLUkGI78\nXkL40m4LBNs5Z4Db5ozBMK/3FNArYiRgMQMTBy6d/khfzrk+RBOj1+pU2oZ14IHL\nywBRticzY0il8499/Lf154QmC/2CUOBGYPSUWYj46pR5noe018FD3NDNjkPSqOKg\n3Tvacx7Ub7GyDU9hEbOc/pTT17UdNUcwia6oYqGHK3gII6fEDd4mXmc2z4awNHIP\n1Y8eXhrIZbDeMu4/oAkn5hCucAYG2x/4j65/z+l+96oqbDhJOUNSsW8VMKEa5AaD\nh1XtRYxwo/8l0xh6Z6LGpT9VqJW3C7OaNzXwA09f8Lg7GXuodJkdxaDV/An90sRQ\npE4gDawHS3AD9FLOZafrgvEdPwayrKkRpD6Cnlt5Wv6/ARhGTIKsPxqDCfoTH/T1\n8yeqFA9SNncEZKMs+eT/sXH344iTIFzxh2D3aBFPlgtvIDkJ5urq69CUnwmGjx5l\nw2BGYhvG0DI+SYugrbDvhxDxd2Lafjwi/Y9NPkWv5OaRwD6o+MquNG9ivZaMDtYA\nB7k6cx0igoMNY3Z45Z4lZcsg8H8Y+P3wTW3ydkTY/99zLkPX1heh2nRi2iRVK1iq\nYYP5RRLUGvVWn3KNnnUS\n=CE1E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T13:21:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/d5cbc44e1069fd0e95c373d971bb25caa6f3fd14","node_id":"C_kwDOE9xoStoAKGQ1Y2JjNDRlMTA2OWZkMGU5NWMzNzNkOTcxYmIyNWNhYTZmM2ZkMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f","sha":"280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f"}],"sha":"d5cbc44e1069fd0e95c373d971bb25caa6f3fd14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/d5cbc44e1069fd0e95c373d971bb25caa6f3fd14"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4548045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Nexucis","id":4548045,"login":"Nexucis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDgwNDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:01:31Z","email":"husson.augustin@gmail.com","name":"Augustin Husson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:01:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[BUGFIX] harden the headers of the datasource proxy responses (#4558)\n\n* [BUGFIX] secure the datasource proxy responses served under the Perses origin\n\nThe response of a datasource is served by the proxy under the origin of Perses.\nA datasource (or anyone controlling its response) could therefore run scripts with the\nsession of a user opening a link to it, set the Perses cookies, or redirect to any website.\n\nEvery proxied response now:\n- gets \"Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src ''none''; frame-ancestors ''none''\"\n  and \"X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\"\n- loses the headers that would apply to the Perses origin: Set-Cookie(2), Clear-Site-Data,\n  Refresh, Strict-Transport-Security, Alt-Svc, Service-Worker-Allowed and the CORS headers\n  (the CORS policy is defined by security.cors)\n- only keeps the relative Location / Content-Location headers\n\nThe UI and the plugins query the proxy with fetch, for which the browser ignores the CSP of\nthe response, so there is no functional impact on Perses.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] clarify why the Set-Cookie header of the datasource response is removed\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"093f7d11373f1fd0fb876d358473b94d692e3552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/093f7d11373f1fd0fb876d358473b94d692e3552"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f","verification":{"payload":"tree 093f7d11373f1fd0fb876d358473b94d692e3552\nparent ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b\nauthor Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com> 1791367291 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791367291 +0000\n\n[BUGFIX] harden the headers of the datasource proxy responses (#4558)\n\n* [BUGFIX] secure the datasource proxy responses served under the Perses origin\n\nThe response of a datasource is served by the proxy under the origin of Perses.\nA datasource (or anyone controlling its response) could therefore run scripts with the\nsession of a user opening a link to it, set the Perses cookies, or redirect to any website.\n\nEvery proxied response now:\n- gets \"Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src ''none''; frame-ancestors ''none''\"\n  and \"X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\"\n- loses the headers that would apply to the Perses origin: Set-Cookie(2), Clear-Site-Data,\n  Refresh, Strict-Transport-Security, Alt-Svc, Service-Worker-Allowed and the CORS headers\n  (the CORS policy is defined by security.cors)\n- only keeps the relative Location / Content-Location headers\n\nThe UI and the plugins query the proxy with fetch, for which the browser ignores the CSP of\nthe response, so there is no functional impact on Perses.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] clarify why the Set-Cookie header of the datasource response is removed\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhiLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbogQAFd82DDOCI5tyRtsq1+jPbMn\nMLRb1szXSUtxwYP4WBa/ZTzgLp0XTQuQ58M2ecgj4qSHjhJF9NG4iBVN5Kc0ABeE\nFFx3mKs2KgCI6deKI5MXBvsFfm8klotO3wpsUcOt0qhayvUsbZtDN27o41mVUs3I\nCiiVcklyOLJ7MFVIYRtrsRKUSqgdKhb9DbMYS6ys/i28RKKf5AhnT8OmZakIVbEQ\natmlyurI3j8jxmTyMngYCoUIeiURXu4NKYMLUpO7LG5kX5in0laNdWlfvlOzwend\n3gpcKIeZawXqvMUke5XKAigknWJHUYJ+bnFpYifCQc1YuhqLV/bdRwPvoU9reDpi\n3MrArVS9bvuxbW4BfOOw1/h9D+ocUkHen1PkbqF+I6mXHmdULBUg2PXElTxQo1tM\nyP7aBZU6aihSCp6M94x1ei9ynWoSB5ZV2fN6fjoud967C38R0HfFrzpeTXcDr4mq\nMF6KBfCZ2aO5pGWOet2KpX3qso/v40jOuuzqvqsF85QdstNJUcTtoztscKs5Eb/g\nl97EL++pIFqd0D6oaoTPo3suDGMu0ltD+CVAb3mIHtpKMKr88RH2Na2ABe1S2udX\nJjnRqq863dqzcTZ+vCu7QFisqHF/wn3rRgXrYwb7D6nLxV0tL4RQ/9xvc1Vb4lWD\noBiiFVk9wKJYiELW2OT6\n=K54R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:01:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f","node_id":"C_kwDOE9xoStoAKDI4MGVjMjFiZDQ5ZmM1MTE2N2I0MTcyZDUzYzExMTM0MmE1NTk3NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b","sha":"ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b"}],"sha":"280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/280ec21bd49fc51167b4172d53c111342a55975f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5708692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asergeant01","id":5708692,"login":"asergeant01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MDg2OTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:29:56Z","email":"alan.sergeant@sap.com","name":"Alan Sergeant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:29:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[ENHANCEMENT] Add NewSelector convenience constructor to go-sdk/datasource (#4557)\n\nNewSelector(kind, name) auto-detects a \"$\" prefix and delegates to\nNewVariableSelector for variable references or NewStaticSelector for\nconcrete datasources. This lets plugin query/variable option functions\nmake a single call instead of duplicating the HasPrefix(\"$\") guard.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alan Sergeant <alan.sergeant@sap.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe82285b45a708c1ad90882e256f447d0e61f2a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/fe82285b45a708c1ad90882e256f447d0e61f2a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b","verification":{"payload":"tree fe82285b45a708c1ad90882e256f447d0e61f2a3\nparent 153b920a7f0f2c830d93377e625d69767abe9163\nauthor Alan Sergeant <alan.sergeant@sap.com> 1791365396 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791365396 +0000\n\n[ENHANCEMENT] Add NewSelector convenience constructor to go-sdk/datasource (#4557)\n\nNewSelector(kind, name) auto-detects a \"$\" prefix and delegates to\nNewVariableSelector for variable references or NewStaticSelector for\nconcrete datasources. This lets plugin query/variable option functions\nmake a single call instead of duplicating the HasPrefix(\"$\") guard.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alan Sergeant <alan.sergeant@sap.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhEkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYEgQACBQUDY2aUtHAltna7KuAqoz\nu279grPx6iTKg53sSRs8kRP0B7SaoN8m2mOnpF3bLKzH8emTZUk9AZURdplAPU2n\nKs7mahy9O9Nj1PRJEnIGleYZAkplH+++7HobyPOBxTjqOQDMsMN1dO7S6hOBxHRP\nnm//vg+oJewEe61IpHm38BUw9HWPbecbpKuP0Xo65MlBg+Aw7gqWyog66u43b3DD\n6CutjkjbkMEZ7ZBsljxhNIESRuDpJr4yWf02ty/u2u1obNwwsJlJFMSQti3F/y/N\nwwhrRDXVXxDqF0wfmMAQanBzautIdWKCFnMxCMilBJ5M1fSG5lpKnBVJlKmDWHBM\nZj+4pxvEK654t5o4dDAStrouWKni54GGe4enzONsKq2VvKogpxWEGbyOuTYzTWZs\ndoaa9+ygVy3omJ0/I+VddiB6SEDKSCtViu0LKmjG4OfyKjew19pvSAHqL2ehBv6Y\nihmvR5k2QVF6gPsUOljln7orMQaiEI4+3oWNkdvhufB48zh2lIQgKAPTwRefVqJh\nqsMrvQTbHKZHFQSP8TDWpmRqHTnxGFgZmTAyYOHJCBwcFYluQoj3XlVO4iGs6ozx\nCmmtk1ClErP3aztKIgPOnjkuIcrRkQzRe+8y0tHxF3Uojxe0apeYP6egTp5iZ6zQ\nPMwY/vqIJ9Ge33FjOvc+\n=QIEr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:30:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b","node_id":"C_kwDOE9xoStoAKGRkZmY0MTFmNmExMDQ5ODdkYzM5NmE3ZDYwYWIzZjRhMmM1ZDhmMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/153b920a7f0f2c830d93377e625d69767abe9163","sha":"153b920a7f0f2c830d93377e625d69767abe9163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/153b920a7f0f2c830d93377e625d69767abe9163"}],"sha":"ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/ddff411f6a104987dc396a7d60ab3f4a2c5d8f2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5708692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asergeant01","id":5708692,"login":"asergeant01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MDg2OTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asergeant01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/153b920a7f0f2c830d93377e625d69767abe9163/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:33:35Z","email":"asergeant01@gmail.com","name":"Alan Sergeant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:33:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[BUGFIX] Emit datasource variable references as plain JSON/YAML strings (#4545)\n\nWhen a Go SDK caller passes a datasource Name starting with \"$\" (or\n\"${...}\"), MarshalJSON and MarshalYAML now emit it as a plain string\n(e.g. \"$myDatasource\") instead of a structured {\"kind\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\nobject. Perses resolves plain-string selectors as variable references at\nruntime, so the structured form was causing the selector to resolve to\nno data.\n\nThe Selector struct keeps its Kind and Name fields unchanged, preserving\nbackwards compatibility with existing struct literals and field accesses.\nTwo convenience constructors are added:\n  - NewStaticSelector(kind, name) for concrete datasources\n  - NewVariableSelector(name) for variable references, with validation\n    against the same regex as CUE (rejects pure-numeric names to avoid\n    collision with PromQL positional-syntax $1/$2)\n\nBoth JSON and YAML round-trips are covered. Non-string YAML scalars\n(!!int, !!bool) in the selector position are rejected with a descriptive\nerror.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alan Sergeant <alan.sergeant@sap.com>","tree":{"sha":"127f3105204f26c2855876c15c638d5b733eff53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/127f3105204f26c2855876c15c638d5b733eff53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/153b920a7f0f2c830d93377e625d69767abe9163","verification":{"payload":"tree 127f3105204f26c2855876c15c638d5b733eff53\nparent de4d31844d87b25749f4011a7d608d60b7ce0909\nauthor Alan Sergeant <asergeant01@gmail.com> 1791304415 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791304415 +0200\n\n[BUGFIX] Emit datasource variable references as plain JSON/YAML strings (#4545)\n\nWhen a Go SDK caller passes a datasource Name starting with \"$\" (or\n\"${...}\"), MarshalJSON and MarshalYAML now emit it as a plain string\n(e.g. \"$myDatasource\") instead of a structured {\"kind\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\nobject. Perses resolves plain-string selectors as variable references at\nruntime, so the structured form was causing the selector to resolve to\nno data.\n\nThe Selector struct keeps its Kind and Name fields unchanged, preserving\nbackwards compatibility with existing struct literals and field accesses.\nTwo convenience constructors are added:\n  - NewStaticSelector(kind, name) for concrete datasources\n  - NewVariableSelector(name) for variable references, with validation\n    against the same regex as CUE (rejects pure-numeric names to avoid\n    collision with PromQL positional-syntax $1/$2)\n\nBoth JSON and YAML round-trips are covered. Non-string YAML scalars\n(!!int, !!bool) in the selector position are rejected with a descriptive\nerror.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alan Sergeant <alan.sergeant@sap.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxSLfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWG4QAGqGWdfxCJcDwIfumR9kLIuI\n5l+mmxVkCxl7xjyt5sIRGsFbTV5g7ytCawoGRq47uZw4YAvfqzV8EIoLyImHv2zi\nmqoEDEdyue+HvQ9qaGbEHMKjq9hOMT936IUY8XuwrsY620IV10RVZurnf/6Hu/AY\nrqWmG+McPxoRc+upqCdyVeWpKClDTMlQuUH7cXRFBAgmAH/NWJCFid15nJn0YTUh\necqKdic3Py6Wq3pibnhfv4NKUBsHjdg/AJdlww2u+ywRIdhfLusC3ZhUlfjWETvL\nTV3dNhuYNDF1k09VTyKca3Xl