d69767abe9163"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/369290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajusem","id":369290,"login":"rajusem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTI5MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajusem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/de4d31844d87b25749f4011a7d608d60b7ce0909/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:20:32Z","email":"rzalavad@redhat.com","name":"Raj Zalavadia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:20:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[ENHANCEMENT] Grafana migration: keep the default time range, refresh interval and timezone (#4555)\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] Grafana migration: keep the default time range, refresh interval and timezone\n\nThe migration of a Grafana dashboard always set the duration to 1h and\ndropped the refresh interval and the timezone. It now keeps them when\nPerses can express them:\n\n- time range: from now-<duration> to now, or to a past now-<delay>,\n  becomes the default duration. Months, quarters and years become days\n  (30, 90, 365): Perses has no month or quarter unit, and a\n  PersesDashboard custom resource rejects the y unit. A dashboard\n  without a time range gets 6h, like in Grafana. Any other time range\n  falls back to 1h.\n- refresh: kept when it is a duration, otherwise no auto-refresh.\n- timezone: utc becomes UTC and IANA names are kept. browser and the\n  empty value leave the timezone unset.\n\nThe three fields are decoded best-effort, so a value of an unexpected\ntype (e.g. \"refresh\": false from older Grafana versions) never makes\nthe migration fail.\n\nCloses #1531\n\nSigned-off-by: Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com>\n\n* Address review: drop docs section, keep ms refresh, read now-d as 1d\n\n- docs/migration.md: remove the \"What is migrated\" section, as asked in\n  the review: the migration is best-effort, and the release note will\n  mention the time settings. The example of docs/cli.md stays updated.\n- Keep a refresh interval in milliseconds, e.g. 500ms: Grafana''s\n  interval parser accepts the ms unit, and so does a Perses duration.\n  A time range still can''t use it, as in Grafana''s date math.\n- Read a missing count in a relative time as 1, like Grafana''s date\n  math: now-d means now-1d, and gives 1d instead of 1h.\n\nSigned-off-by: Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com>","tree":{"sha":"dabfc8aa153abafdd818cfb3337f82557716f161","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/dabfc8aa153abafdd818cfb3337f82557716f161"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/de4d31844d87b25749f4011a7d608d60b7ce0909","verification":{"payload":"tree dabfc8aa153abafdd818cfb3337f82557716f161\nparent d3f0c13a2cdf261e96cc4381ddb490b306a23c1f\nauthor Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com> 1791300032 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791300032 +0000\n\n[ENHANCEMENT] Grafana migration: keep the default time range, refresh interval and timezone (#4555)\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] Grafana migration: keep the default time range, refresh interval and timezone\n\nThe migration of a Grafana dashboard always set the duration to 1h and\ndropped the refresh interval and the timezone. It now keeps them when\nPerses can express them:\n\n- time range: from now-<duration> to now, or to a past now-<delay>,\n  becomes the default duration. Months, quarters and years become days\n  (30, 90, 365): Perses has no month or quarter unit, and a\n  PersesDashboard custom resource rejects the y unit. A dashboard\n  without a time range gets 6h, like in Grafana. Any other time range\n  falls back to 1h.\n- refresh: kept when it is a duration, otherwise no auto-refresh.\n- timezone: utc becomes UTC and IANA names are kept. browser and the\n  empty value leave the timezone unset.\n\nThe three fields are decoded best-effort, so a value of an unexpected\ntype (e.g. \"refresh\": false from older Grafana versions) never makes\nthe migration fail.\n\nCloses #1531\n\nSigned-off-by: Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com>\n\n* Address review: drop docs section, keep ms refresh, read now-d as 1d\n\n- docs/migration.md: remove the \"What is migrated\" section, as asked in\n  the review: the migration is best-effort, and the release note will\n  mention the time settings. The example of docs/cli.md stays updated.\n- Keep a refresh interval in milliseconds, e.g. 500ms: Grafana''s\n  interval parser accepts the ms unit, and so does a Perses duration.\n  A time range still can''t use it, as in Grafana''s date math.\n- Read a missing count in a relative time as 1, like Grafana''s date\n  math: now-d means now-1d, and gives 1d instead of 1h.\n\nSigned-off-by: Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Raj Zalavadia <rzalavad@redhat.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRHQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQL8QAA9eLCvCRnwJQfuomiiRxtmb\nn6V4LShpMEroaKnbUWR32pBifnmIVwGM7/ybVf0HfAt7t9rVG9wQiv5zZPMWEkgO\noPEBnrzC1p3aiwdiuYrrIqnl/xdnozNhZ2fXnS3z+PgCAUaAWB9sWM7nTF1m4lM0\n5I1M41NXMa1cQuPOynAbDNTWfreZapD5U+dS3FBkn4S/kNHVNGGXrSG9zXO3wjEX\nACIkIjBxMmoooGYsMwTMHPUsYuuQBF56mE/d6uTHlJBzGfSJHvKQbzalFZ8kegKz\nwYakIwgq7iSECYKkdPW4pQl3RCQGP2dHKZp