ts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Nexucis","id":4548045,"login":"Nexucis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDgwNDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexucis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/e18b35ae90c1dab1df3ccee7f0b5c2c2a2e59914/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:36:07Z","email":"husson.augustin@gmail.com","name":"Augustin Husson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:36:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[ENHANCEMENT] proxy: reuse HTTP transport per saved datasource (#4521)\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: reuse HTTP transport per saved datasource\n\nPreviously, a new http.Transport was created for every proxied request, so no connection (TCP + TLS) was ever reused, and each discarded transport kept its idle connections open until IdleConnTimeout.\nThe transport is now cached per saved datasource (global, project and dashboard scopes), keyed by the datasource identity and a hash of the TLS config of its secret. A transport is rebuilt when the TLS config changes or after 5 minutes, so certificate files rotated on disk are picked up. Unsaved datasources are not cached.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: make MaxConnsPerHost configurable\n\nAdd datasource.http_proxy.max_conns_per_host to limit the number of connections Perses opens, per datasource, to a given host. Zero (default) means no limit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] proxy: add a benchmark for the transport cache\n\nCompare the cost of proxying a request with a new transport per request (previous behavior, still used for unsaved datasources) and with the cached transport, over HTTP and HTTPS.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: make the idle connection limits configurable\n\nAdd datasource.http_proxy.max_idle_conns (default 100) and datasource.http_proxy.max_idle_conns_per_host (default 10). As there is one transport per datasource, they bound the number of idle connections, and so the sockets and memory, kept per datasource. It can be lowered when running Perses with a large number of datasources.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: detect the rotation of the CA file on disk\n\nThe CA file is only read when the transport is built. It is now stat''ed on each request, and the transport is rebuilt when its modification time or size changes. If the rebuild fails while the TLS config didn''t change, the previous transport is still used for up to 1 minute, retrying at most every 5s.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* fix windows tests\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"fab2d657eb0aec3a8d0c0f1aeccfc9cd1ce0875e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/fab2d657eb0aec3a8d0c0f1aeccfc9cd1ce0875e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/e18b35ae90c1dab1df3ccee7f0b5c2c2a2e59914","verification":{"payload":"tree fab2d657eb0aec3a8d0c0f1aeccfc9cd1ce0875e\nparent b88bc4022d5b25cd7ec199f4655b9a391d6092fc\nauthor Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com> 1790678167 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790678167 +0000\n\n[ENHANCEMENT] proxy: reuse HTTP transport per saved datasource (#4521)\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: reuse HTTP transport per saved datasource\n\nPreviously, a new http.Transport was created for every proxied request, so no connection (TCP + TLS) was ever reused, and each discarded transport kept its idle connections open until IdleConnTimeout.\nThe transport is now cached per saved datasource (global, project and dashboard scopes), keyed by the datasource identity and a hash of the TLS config of its secret. A transport is rebuilt when the TLS config changes or after 5 minutes, so certificate files rotated on disk are picked up. Unsaved datasources are not cached.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: make MaxConnsPerHost configurable\n\nAdd datasource.http_proxy.max_conns_per_host to limit the number of connections Perses opens, per datasource, to a given host. Zero (default) means no limit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [IGNORE] proxy: add a benchmark for the transport cache\n\nCompare the cost of proxying a request with a new transport per request (previous behavior, still used for unsaved datasources) and with the cached transport, over HTTP and HTTPS.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: make the idle connection limits configurable\n\nAdd datasource.http_proxy.max_idle_conns (default 100) and datasource.http_proxy.max_idle_conns_per_host (default 10). As there is one transport per datasource, they bound the number of idle connections, and so the sockets and memory, kept per datasource. It can be lowered when running Perses with a large number of datasources.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] proxy: detect the rotation of the CA file on disk\n\nThe CA file is only read when the transport is built. It is now stat''ed on each request, and the transport is rebuilt when its modification time or size changes. If the rebuild fails while the TLS config didn''t change, the previous transport is still used for up to 1 minute, retrying at most every 5s.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n* fix windows tests\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu5SnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA35YQAKL17NVWYD1nVUqA7HtwOr4+\nzijATVUXxrVP6oWPbIaGlO2dT24vg+ByIIs0Grbf9UNLFM5AQhNTzPiyup9ZlQlm\nDQQTz3mR8tqrZwFovKhn7j1uAPqmIbQ+IgQO12gq9vUFypAyMKwHeA0r9chFMTl9\n0Ha4F0mXqkvUzvKAw7qeO2W+s2PvrZfItg5mFYCzTg81YmIJ88Vt3L3i9hDK0VjK\nS2Yana5ObGYGU0EmNZFDJ74PkOPMjVMgWQO2+6x6ibvf4h0JGycka9n6PjZpIcOE\nVe6uTJgdC0dlfg2yR1V2lqgNO44m5PNakjmE2bxNvRn78meRBNswM8cLbBLEcnqq\nlCDEMtE8/8K7XvAsmr8ZIAUfhRJYWcMjhUrRAlciJ3hF6u/y0Pr6IfeXvegSuVeG\nE8W4ORMBUfv/+3oDBR3vKD4P3WEpvqxjyoQX1xZY2IpJOirxzOfQCebZIhOfy6nh\ntHP8twQNisomNHxy3WaV5cty0YtiwLKkE/BayWJnJQg1VF2lXd4M9Rp4/ubPPstY\nQCSIMFdSsN1tL+Y9BdPnYF0CdMjviWWVXQjhrDg2C69jsTnfk60XvGIFj+AWWHUR\nFWoCvoNTofJuOLDSNHt7VEPnMj63y7c5LODB0BJ9wIOlClSdFTqCVP4hnLAezzK+\n8oGQUjVeIqmhjkkWe/ZU\n=kFBV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:36:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.co