keyFile), allowing a user\nable to create a secret to exfiltrate arbitrary files through the datasource proxy.\n\nFile references are now only allowed in directories listed in the new\n`security.secret_file_allowed_directories` config. Symlinks are resolved and\npaths are checked both when saving a secret and before it is used by the proxy.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: file references in secrets are rejected by default. Existing\nsetups relying on them must configure `security.secret_file_allowed_directories`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd92d891b79439905684b2042a1cfae5792a4cba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/bd92d891b79439905684b2042a1cfae5792a4cba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/bb8fd34543376c66784fd34740180349f0366434","verification":{"payload":"tree bd92d891b79439905684b2042a1cfae5792a4cba\nparent f210ef377ffed7432eacfd72150892318c5c6d7a\nauthor Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com> 1790166788 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790166788 +0200\n\n[BREAKINGCHANGE] restrict files referenced in secrets to allowed directories (#4503)\n\nSecrets and GlobalSecrets could reference any file on the server (passwordFile,\ncredentialsFile, clientSecretFile, caFile, certFile, keyFile), allowing a user\nable to create a secret to exfiltrate arbitrary files through the datasource proxy.\n\nFile references are now only allowed in directories listed in the new\n`security.secret_file_allowed_directories` config. Symlinks are resolved and\npaths are checked both when saving a secret and before it is used by the proxy.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: file references in secrets are rejected by default. Existing\nsetups relying on them must configure `security.secret_file_allowed_directories`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Augustin Husson <husson.augustin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs8cECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArzgQAKV/khHTTE0EkQ8mcmaCT