GNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T06:49:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/52fbeb4fb8dccf47bfb6c18b458866e3e5be451a","node_id":"C_kwDOE9xoStoAKDUyZmJlYjRmYjhkY2NmNDdiZmI2YzE4YjQ1ODg2NmUzZTViZTQ1MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23","sha":"1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23"}],"sha":"52fbeb4fb8dccf47bfb6c18b458866e3e5be451a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/52fbeb4fb8dccf47bfb6c18b458866e3e5be451a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10557236?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pujitha24","id":10557236,"login":"pujitha24","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTU3MjM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:35:46Z","email":"pujitha.rathna@gmail.com","name":"Pujitha Paladugu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:35:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[ENHANCEMENT] Add Cache-Control headers for static UI assets (#4475)\n\nMotivation:\nStatic JS/CSS bundles served by the embedded Go frontend server are\nbuilt with a content hash in their filename (e.g. main.<hash>.js, via\nui/app/rspack.config.mjs''s [name].[contenthash].js), so a given\nfilename''s content never changes across a build. The server was not\nsetting any Cache-Control header for these files, so browsers could\nnot cache them long-term and had to re-fetch them on every load.\n\nApproach:\n- In assetHandler, set Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000,\n  immutable for files matching the existing .js/.css substring check\n  already used there for placeholder replacement.\n- In serveASTFiles, set Cache-Control: no-cache for index.html, since\n  it references the current hashed bundle filenames and must always\n  be revalidated so a client doesn''t keep using stale asset\n  references after a new deploy.\n\nValidation:\nRan `go build ./...` and `go test ./ui/... -v`, all passing, including\ntwo new/updated tests (TestAssetHandlerCacheControl and an added\nassertion in TestServeASTFilesContentType) that fail without this\nchange (previously Cache-Control was always empty) and pass with it.\nAlso ran `golangci-lint run ./ui/...` (0 issues) and `gofmt -l` on the\nchanged files (no output).\n\nReport: https://github.com/perses/perses/issues/4474\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-5 (via Claude Code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"eadf18b719e4f6d8c1384e81fb7c54fc21bfd0f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/eadf18b719e4f6d8c1384e81fb7c54fc21bfd0f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23","verification":{"payload":"tree eadf18b719e4f6d8c1384e81fb7c54fc21bfd0f7\nparent dc382e12e4755babe5a81ce132f3f461b83b1a6d\nauthor Pujitha Paladugu <pujitha.rathna@gmail.com> 1789713346 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789713346 +0000\n\n[ENHANCEMENT] Add Cache-Control headers for static UI assets (#4475)\n\nMotivation:\nStatic JS/CSS bundles served by the embedded Go frontend server are\nbuilt with a content hash in their filename (e.g. main.<hash>.js, via\nui/app/rspack.config.mjs''s [name].[contenthash].js), so a given\nfilename''s content never changes across a build. The server was not\nsetting any Cache-Control header for these files, so browsers could\nnot cache them long-term and had to re-fetch them on every load.\n\nApproach:\n- In assetHandler, set Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000,\n  immutable for files matching the existing .js/.css substring check\n  already used there for placeholder replacement.\n- In serveASTFiles, set Cache-Control: no-cache for index.html, since\n  it references the current hashed bundle filenames and must always\n  be revalidated so a client doesn''t keep using stale asset\n  references after a new deploy.\n\nValidation:\nRan `go build ./...` and `go test ./ui/... -v`, all passing, including\ntwo new/updated tests (TestAssetHandlerCacheControl and an added\nassertion in TestServeASTFilesContentType) that fail without this\nchange (previously Cache-Control was always empty) and pass with it.\nAlso ran `golangci-lint run ./ui/...` (0 issues) and `gofmt -l` on the\nchanged files (no output).\n\nReport: https://github.com/perses/perses/issues/4474\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-5 (via Claude Code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrNvTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO58QAAaq9K/Rfy98VkIKROLFj5GS\nsAAcXlHl/gyEMMzYAC4lg4rI1hk4rxLOkvTopgfry6HONMZpLP6N0rvbvSbTjd65\nrpHg+wUfWb6gudaDYbEcX+tn0VrRwW1QGLotZoLtoA0XNMMyT3jd/STgaPAI1iJ8\nvwat4rb3X/Fun8T9JJdMDz7EEPbfTrb6wKhufAjJ+xJQ5ObAM7OWOM8G2Qb2joNL\nw44/ccyUKG6T7M2g/EaTKn4lOkHp7gbxpVv90GIhcroZDibqDVuvwgMYVYLOMmgv\nECjcTfDQS5u5xnxPwMpjMguvkvPcNvcrZ1eDMMBqr1Y/ME6kPM97uh2UF3Z7KKTE\nfcYYfpSnTvCwHOn21dVLu9f8nCQ6Pm4FficpAtokRNqbJupYGgM8TaT0n0pSt+we\nC5alMFohI956D9eE3AlAJVK/dKvWnV63QhOlM+LAVKuAX0BPVot48/dUrArjFr+e\nBZr1bKiX4ukKUCe7V87RSOkIBB43UA4lXfxQIC6zPc8h7uJmWelBZ9HrCuh7xwcw\nQ5MgVJFxAdnhlhhncVJKdcoHvkJtXCca39aOqTG1BD5wNUtAVO/UznpmTsoWXPmE\nXudHpQnkdEpholbttaxMCbBSSKj6xd4gCOgR1pyVeBRdjYZmQWLcoqWdif+/NcAV\nwvhaDiG98YST3J8LFFWm\n=fQPH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T06:36:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23","node_id":"C_kwDOE9xoStoAKDFlNDkxZDM2NWQwM2JlZWNhNDgxMTU5NGIwNThhNjY4MzllYmZlMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/perses/perses/commit/dc382e12e4755babe5a81ce132f3f461b83b1a6d","sha":"dc382e12e4755babe5a81ce132f3f461b83b1a6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/dc382e12e4755babe5a81ce132f3f461b83b1a6d"}],"sha":"1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/1e491d365d03beeca4811594b058a66839ebfe23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10557236?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pujitha24","id":10557236,"login":"pujitha24","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTU3MjM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pujitha24","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/commits/dc382e12e4755babe5a81ce132f3f461b83b1a6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:19:25Z","email":"pujitha.rathna@gmail.com","name":"Pujitha Paladugu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:19:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[ENHANCEMENT] Support custom login property for the OIDC provider (#4468)\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] Support custom login property for the OIDC provider\n\nMotivation: The OIDC provider''s GetLogin() always derives the login name\nfrom the email address, falling back to subject. The standard OIDC\npreferred_username claim is already parsed into\nexternalUserInfoProfile.PreferredUsername but was never used. The OAuth\nprovider already supports selecting the login field via\ncustom_login_property; OIDC had no equivalent, making it impossible to\nkeep login names consistent when migrating between OAuth and OIDC, or to\nuse preferred_username with IdPs (e.g. Keycloak) where it differs from\nthe email prefix.\n\nApproach: Add a CustomLoginProperty field to config.OIDCProvider,\nmirroring the OAuth provider''s existing option. oidcUserInfo.GetLogin()\nnow checks this configured property first (restricted to the userinfo\nfields Perses already parses: name, given_name, family_name,\nmiddle_name, nickname, preferred_username, email), and only falls back\nto the email-then-subject behavior if the property is unset or empty in\nthe response. This is opt-in and defaults to empty, so existing\ndeployments keep their current login names unless they explicitly set\nthe new option. Documented the new option in\ndocs/configuration/configuration.md.\n\nValidation: go build ./internal/api/impl/auth/... ./pkg/model/api/config/...\nand go test ./internal/api/impl/auth/... ./pkg/model/api/config/... pass,\nincluding a new TestOIDCUserInfoGetLogin table test that fails without\nthe fix (custom-property cases have no other code path to satisfy them)\nand passes with it. Also ran golangci-lint run on both packages (0\nissues), gofmt -l on the changed files (no diff), and\ngo run ./scripts/check-license --check (compliant). Full-repo\n`go build ./...` / `make test` could not be run here because of a\npre-existing, unrelated `ui/endpoint.go:46:35: undefined: embedFS` build\nerror, confirmed present on a clean checkout of this branch before any\nof these changes (requires the UI''s generated embed step). This does not\naffect the backend packages touched by this change.\n\nReport: https://github.com/perses/perses/issues/4456\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-5 (via Claude Code)\n\n* Address review feedback on OIDC custom_login_property\n\n- Turn CustomLoginProperty into a proper LoginProperty enum type\n  (validated on unmarshal), instead of a bare string, per review.\n- Apply suggested getProfileProperty/GetLogin simplification so the\n  \"email\" case and the unset/unknown default both derive the login\n  from the email prefix via buildLoginFromEmail, and simplify GetLogin\n  accordingly.\n- Align the docs entry with the enum documentation convention already\n  used elsewhere in configuration.md (e.g. same_site).\n- Update/add unit tests to match.\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Align custom_login_property doc entry indentation per review\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d03c440d258e10ea4e6d0872a79481615c1108b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/trees/4d03c440d258e10ea4e6d0872a79481615c1108b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/perses/git/commits/dc382e12e4755babe5a81ce132f3f461b83b1a6d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d03c440d258e10ea4e6d0872a79481615c1108b\nparent 25e94a18b57b1e9f73d093cad725637c0c7b12ef\nauthor Pujitha Paladugu <pujitha.rathna@gmail.com> 1789712365 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789712365 +0000\n\n[ENHANCEMENT] Support custom login property for the OIDC provider (#4468)\n\n* [ENHANCEMENT] Support custom login property for the OIDC provider\n\nMotivation: The OIDC provider''s GetLogin() always derives the login name\nfrom the email address, falling back to subject. The standard OIDC\npreferred_username claim is already parsed into\nexternalUserInfoProfile.PreferredUsername but was never used. The OAuth\nprovider already supports selecting the login field via\ncustom_login_property; OIDC had no equivalent, making it impossible to\nkeep login names consistent when migrating between OAuth and OIDC, or to\nuse preferred_username with IdPs (e.g. Keycloak) where it differs from\nthe email prefix.\n\nApproach: Add a CustomLoginProperty field to config.OIDCProvider,\nmirroring the OAuth provider''s existing option. oidcUserInfo.GetLogin()\nnow checks this configured property first (restricted to the userinfo\nfields Perses already parses: name, given_name, family_name,\nmiddle_name, nickname, preferred_username, email), and only falls back\nto the email-then-subject behavior if the property is unset or empty in\nthe response. This is opt-in and defaults to empty, so existing\ndeployments keep their current login names unless they explicitly set\nthe new option. Documented the new option in\ndocs/configuration/configuration.md.\n\nValidation: go build ./internal/api/impl/auth/... ./pkg/model/api/config/...\nand go test ./internal/api/impl/auth/... ./pkg/model/api/config/... pass,\nincluding a new TestOIDCUserInfoGetLogin table test that fails without\nthe fix (custom-property cases have no other code path to satisfy them)\nand passes with it. Also ran golangci-lint run on both packages (0\nissues), gofmt -l on the changed files (no diff), and\ngo run ./scripts/check-license --check (compliant). Full-repo\n`go build ./...` / `make test` could not be run here because of a\npre-existing, unrelated `ui/endpoint.go:46:35: undefined: embedFS` build\nerror, confirmed present on a clean checkout of this branch before any\nof these changes (requires the UI''s generated embed step). This does not\naffect the backend packages touched by this change.\n\nReport: https://github.com/perses/perses/issues/4456\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-5 (via Claude Code)\n\n* Address review feedback on OIDC custom_login_property\n\n- Turn CustomLoginProperty into a proper LoginProperty enum type\n  (validated on unmarshal), instead of a bare string, per review.\n- Apply suggested getProfileProperty/GetLogin simplification so the\n  \"email\" case and the unset/unknown default both derive the login\n  from the email prefix via buildLoginFromEmail, and simplify GetLogin\n  accordingly.\n- Align the docs entry with the enum documentation convention already\n  used elsewhere in configuration.md (e.g. same_site).\n- Update/add unit tests to match.\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Align custom_login_property doc entry indentation per review\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Pujitha Paladugu <10557236+pujitha24@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrNf9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeDoQACHO3mloyo9WRGne6anKbJi2\nhHZypBBHFAW9btlhsJfJ9E54iN/G5YTokeC+m3E9ZIPg8e5hflVVDUBW0OUH5olE\nE2CTzDJXOHVob4vhjuca+DKFSyW1CM9E9DJWA8M9HBVXNtgWxZkfENDGmnXShNvm\narCZprVCmOBnqAuGLifNHYz01tj8C9uX8/1CyzGt439gcK54kpwTc5KoAgYq2kFB\n2TpE/0lzaqxldrUg6g7iy5e+wz5Pvd8/VdLUqgl2hDzQsTB2H9imJtj+btkyqCM9\n3s9fKWzS3rPJc2ljvNzMp4Vcpxi7rI5Ir1lXNvAvpYPOeTF1eoDeAusw2gnkxb2/\n6zBBopnLXD