://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-importer/commit/5bc3f495d1043f3da7104054a7ee0b66095d5eb7","node_id":"C_kwDOFAoDiNoAKDViYzNmNDk1ZDEwNDNmM2RhNzEwNDA1NGE3ZWUwYjY2MDk1ZDVlYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-importer/commit/6e268116cd56ce1b64f81aa45eeec36ca9e01af0","sha":"6e268116cd56ce1b64f81aa45eeec36ca9e01af0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/6e268116cd56ce1b64f81aa45eeec36ca9e01af0"}],"sha":"5bc3f495d1043f3da7104054a7ee0b66095d5eb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/5bc3f495d1043f3da7104054a7ee0b66095d5eb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11871778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ValeriaMaltseva","id":11871778,"login":"ValeriaMaltseva","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODcxNzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/6e268116cd56ce1b64f81aa45eeec36ca9e01af0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:56:31Z","email":"valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com","name":"Valeriia Maltseva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:56:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup) (#690)\n\n* [Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup)\n\nAdopts the packaged-build approach used in studio-ui-bundle and\npimcore-agent-bundle: instead of committing the expanded\nsrc/Resources/public/studio/build/ tree, we commit a single\ncontent-addressed build-dist/build-<id>.zip and let studio-ui-bundle\nreconstruct the build directory at cache warmup. This removes the\nper-build file churn and merge conflicts the \"Automatic frontend\nbuild\" commits used to cause.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Pin reusable Studio Frontend Build workflow to a commit SHA\n\n@main is mutable and this caller grants contents: write, so a compromised\nor accidental upstream branch update could execute with write access to\nthis repository. Pin to the current revision of\nreusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml, keeping main as an update\ncomment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop ineffective merge=ours from build-dist archive attribute\n\nmerge=ours names a custom Git merge driver that isn''t built in and isn''t\nregistered anywhere in this org (no repo configures merge.ours.driver), so\nthe attribute was silently a no-op rather than actually preventing merge\nconflicts on the archive. Document the manual resolution instead: on a\nforward-merge conflict, keep the target branch''s archive and let CI\nregenerate it on the next real source change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clean stale build dirs before building to avoid archiving the wrong one\n\nstudio-package-build selects the lexicographically greatest .build-id it\nfinds on disk, not the one produced by the current run. Without cleanup, a\ndirectory left over from an earlier source state could sort higher than a\nfresh rebuild''s id and get archived instead of it. This bundle has a single\nbuild target (no SDK/app pair sharing a build-id group like studio-ui-bundle\nitself has), so it''s safe to remove every other build dir before building.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7bd8bc6ad2db76e03aaed975cc3c8b4fb849be55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/git/trees/7bd8bc6ad2db76e03aaed975cc3c8b4fb849be55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/git/commits/6e268116cd56ce1b64f81aa45eeec36ca9e01af0","verification":{"payload":"tree 7bd8bc6ad2db76e03aaed975cc3c8b4fb849be55\nparent fb6a72cc7aa85d16d9ea09f26e09a1793a2577ec\nauthor Valeriia Maltseva <valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com> 1788944191 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788944191 +0200\n\n[Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup) (#690)\n\n* [Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup)\n\nAdopts the packaged-build approach used in studio-ui-bundle and\npimcore-agent-bundle: instead of committing the expanded\nsrc/Resources/public/studio/build/ tree, we commit a single\ncontent-addressed build-dist/build-<id>.zip and let studio-ui-bundle\nreconstruct the build directory at cache warmup. This removes the\nper-build file churn and merge conflicts the \"Automatic frontend\nbuild\" commits used to cause.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Pin reusable Studio Frontend Build workflow to a commit SHA\n\n@main is mutable and this caller grants contents: write, so a compromised\nor accidental upstream branch update could execute with write access to\nthis repository. Pin to the current revision of\nreusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml, keeping main as an update\ncomment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop ineffective merge=ours from build-dist archive attribute\n\nmerge=ours names a custom Git merge driver that isn''t built in and isn''t\nregistered anywhere in this org (no repo configures merge.ours.driver), so\nthe attribute was silently a no-op rather than actually preventing merge\nconflicts on the archive. Document the manual resolution instead: on a\nforward-merge conflict, keep the target branch''s archive and let CI\nregenerate it on the next real source change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clean stale build dirs before building to avoid archiving the wrong one\n\nstudio-package-build selects the lexicographically greatest .build-id it\nfinds on disk, not the one produced by the current run. Without cleanup, a\ndirectory left over from an earlier source state could sort higher than a\nfresh rebuild''s id and get archived instead of it. This bundle has a single\nbuild target (no SDK/app pair sharing a build-id group like studio-ui-bundle\nitself has), so it''s safe to remove every other build dir before building.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoR8/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi3kQAJL8aqege4H8Y93wb6pE0fQ6\nyGg8XUI7M0O8B/8Pd8x6QHCzAcSqQwc2nCHbG7SqJQP5Mpku/tvQq8NkQ6K6Fix5\nY62XgnWxAzol2aOjTcpvujzA6qdJ6aFX79ITPMZisaXEC65HfZ06bV