nizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-importer/commit/ff371de278be290207a1e6c79a4ed2e30ea1ef73","node_id":"C_kwDOFAoDiNoAKGZmMzcxZGUyNzhiZTI5MDIwN2ExZTZjNzlhNGVkMmUzMGVhMWVmNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-importer/commit/9824b7361eb0a501c03944301a0f0ede9c9c8d7a","sha":"9824b7361eb0a501c03944301a0f0ede9c9c8d7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/9824b7361eb0a501c03944301a0f0ede9c9c8d7a"}],"sha":"ff371de278be290207a1e6c79a4ed2e30ea1ef73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/ff371de278be290207a1e6c79a4ed2e30ea1ef73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11871778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ValeriaMaltseva","id":11871778,"login":"ValeriaMaltseva","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODcxNzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/9824b7361eb0a501c03944301a0f0ede9c9c8d7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:45:46Z","email":"valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com","name":"Valeriia Maltseva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:45:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio] Fix blank unit selection for the static Quantity Value transformer (#682)\n\n* [Studio] Fix blank unit selection for the static Quantity Value transformer\n\nThe unit select of the Quantity Value transformer was always empty when the\nunit source was set to \"Static\".\n\n`UnitDataResponse` documented its list under the OpenAPI property name\n`UnitList`, while the serializer emits the actual property name `unitList`.\nThe generated API client therefore typed the response as `UnitList` and the\ntransformer form read `unitData?.UnitList`, which was always undefined.\n\nThe schema annotation was already corrected to `unitList`, but the committed\nOpenAPI snapshot and the generated client still carried the old name, so the\ntype checker agreed with the broken access. Refresh the snapshot property,\nregenerate the client and read `unitList` in the transformer form.\n\nConsumers that worked around this by renaming `unitList` back to `UnitList`\nin the response must drop that workaround.\n\nFixes pimcore/platform-version#148\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio] Refresh data-importer OpenAPI snapshot property metadata\n\nThe committed OpenAPI snapshot predated several `#[Property]` annotations in\nthe bundle''s schema classes. The generated API client therefore carried no\ndescriptions for `currentConfig.label` and `userPermissions.update`/`delete`,\nand typed `dataPreview.data` as `any`.\n\nRefresh only the `BundleDataImporter*` schemas in the snapshot — 21 additions,\nall property descriptions and examples plus the `dataPreview.data` string type\n— and regenerate the client. Nothing outside the data-importer schemas is\ntouched, so the snapshot keeps its existing 403 paths and 369 components.\n\n`CalculateTransformationResultTypeParameters::$currentConfig` documents\n`dataSourceIndex` items as `integer`, which contradicts both the frontend\n(string column identifiers throughout) and the bundle''s own\n`ColumnHeadersResponse`, where `id` and `dataIndex` are `string`. That one\nproperty is deliberately left un-refreshed so `dataSourceIndex` stays `any`\nuntil the annotation itself is corrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Studio] Fix dataSourceIndex type mismatch in transformation type calculation\n\nCalculateTransformationResultTypeParameters::$currentConfig documented\ndataSourceIndex items as integer, contradicting the string column\nidentifiers used throughout the frontend (types.ts''s MappingConfigItem,\nColumnHeadersResponse) and both callers of the generated query\n(advanced-mapping-modal.tsx, use-auto-recalculate-type.ts).\n\nThe last OpenAPI snapshot refresh regenerated this property from the\nPHP annotation, narrowing the generated type from `any` to `number[]`\nand breaking `tsc --noEmit` with TS2345 at advanced-mapping-modal.tsx:80.\n\nCorrect the annotation to `string`, refresh the snapshot for this one\nproperty, and regenerate the client.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio] Automate OpenAPI snapshot refresh with known-drift protection\n\ndocs.jsonopenapi.json was previously updated by manually saving a fetch\nfrom a running Studio instance, then running build-api-client. That\nmanual step has no safeguard against the source instance lagging behind\nthis repo''s own #[Property] annotations, which is exactly how the\ndataSourceIndex integer/string regression (59ee843) got reintroduced.\n\nAdd fetch-and-patch-docs.mjs, run via `npm run fetch-api-docs` (or the\ncombined `npm run update-api-client`, which also regenerates the client\nand typechecks). It fetches STUDIO_API_DOCS_URL, applies a small list of\nknown corrections for cases where the source instance hasn''t caught up\nyet, and fails loudly if a correction''s target shape can no longer be\nfound (signalling the upstream schema changed and the correction needs\nreview) or logs when a correction has become a no-op and can be removed.\n\nSeeded with the dataSourceIndex correction. Verified end-to-end against\nhttps://bugfix.nightly.pimcore.app/pimcore-studio/api/docs/json?locale=en,\nwhich still returns the old integer shape: the script corrected it,\nbuild-api-client regenerated an identical data-importer-api-slice.gen.ts\nto the one already on this branch, and check-types passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio] Drop automated OpenAPI drift-correction script\n\nRemove fetch-and-patch-docs.mjs and its npm scripts. Re-verified the fix\nmanually instead: fetched docs.jsonopenapi.json fresh from\nhttps://bugfix.nightly.pimcore.app/pimcore-studio/api/docs/json?locale=en\n(still typing dataSourceIndex items as integer, since that instance\nhasn''t redeployed the CalculateTransformationResultTypeParameters.php fix\nfrom 59ee843 yet), regenerated the client, confirmed TS2345 reappears at\nadvanced-mapping-modal.tsx:80, then corrected the dataSourceIndex items\ntype back to string in the snapshot and regenerated again. Both files\ncame out identical to what''s already committed, and check-types is clean\nof the dataSourceIndex error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio] Fix incorrect string narrowing of DataPreviewResponse.dataPreview[].data\n\nSame PR (307aeb9, \"fix errors form schema validation\") that introduced the\ndataSourceIndex integer bug also typed dataPreview[].data as string, where\nthe original definition (7c7d95a) left it untyped on purpose.\n\nPreviewData::getDataPreview() forwards each interpreter value unchanged\n(src/Preview/Model/PreviewData.php:52-57); JsonFileInterpreter reads rows\nstraight from json_decode, so a cell''s value can be a string, number,\nboolean, array, object, or null. The frontend already accounts for this at\nevery consumer of the generated type: normalize-data-row.ts explicitly\nstringifies non-string values, preview-import-step.tsx:157 does the same,\nand use-preview-record-query.ts:114 casts the response to\nArray<Record<string, any>> to escape the incorrect string type.\n\nReverted the annotation to unconstrained (no `type` key = arbitrary JSON\nvalue per JSON Schema), matching the pre-307aeb9 shape, and patched the\nsnapshot + regenerated the client the same way as 59ee843 since\nbugfix.nightly.pimcore.app has not redeployed this fix yet. check-types\nis unaffected outside the intended `data?: any` change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ValeriaMaltseva <11871778+ValeriaMaltseva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca3b74031addb627ea1e982da0f48199439bb63c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/git/trees/ca3b74031addb627ea1e982da0f48199439bb63c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/git/commits/9824b7361eb0a501c03944301a0f0ede9c9c8d7a","verification":{"payload":"tree ca3b74031addb627ea1e982da0f48199439bb63