actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-importer/commit/6fe6758faed850f377fd985c68ddb3f130188e26","node_id":"C_kwDOFAoDiNoAKDZmZTY3NThmYWVkODUwZjM3N2ZkOTg1YzY4ZGRiM2YxMzAxODhlMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-importer/commit/2f45178858844d8162ea02232d7dd9d03adebe79","sha":"2f45178858844d8162ea02232d7dd9d03adebe79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/2f45178858844d8162ea02232d7dd9d03adebe79"}],"sha":"6fe6758faed850f377fd985c68ddb3f130188e26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/6fe6758faed850f377fd985c68ddb3f130188e26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138690998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/idaiv","id":138690998,"login":"idaiv","node_id":"U_kgDOCERBtg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/commits/2f45178858844d8162ea02232d7dd9d03adebe79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:48:36Z","email":"138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"idaiv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:48:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Data Importer] Highlight the expanded mapping and align its destination column (#685)\n\n* [Data Importer] Highlight the expanded mapping and align its destination column\n\nHighlights the open mapping section. Collapsed and expanded sections looked\nidentical apart from the chevron, so nothing marked the one being edited. The\nexpanded panel now carries the primary border from the design.\n\nThe rule needs !important. The SDK draws the panel border from\n.ant-collapse.collapse-item--theme-default.collapse-item--bordered, which\noutranks the wrapper selector, and it is a border shorthand rather than a\nborder-color. The drag-and-drop rules alongside it are !important for the same\nreason and are one class more specific, so dragging still takes over the border\nwhile it is in progress.\n\nSwaps the settings gear for the transformation icon on the Advanced button and\non the badge that sits above the arrow when an advanced setup exists, matching\nthe design. The badge was already wired to isAdvanced and only had the wrong\nicon. The icon already ships in the studio-ui-bundle library, so nothing has to\nbe added there. arrowGearIcon is renamed to arrowAdvancedIcon to match what it\nnow renders.\n\nAligns the advanced destination text with the rest of the row. It used\nfontSizeSM, which resolves to 10px against the 12px every control around it\nuses, and it filled only its line box at the top of the slot, so it sat above\nthe vertical center of the source Select and the arrow. It now uses fontSize\nand occupies the same controlHeight box as the Select it replaces, centered\nwithin it. The \"Requires advanced setup\" hint shares that slot and had both\nproblems, so it follows the same rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Center the destination text when the source Select wraps\n\nThe applied suggestion added flex: 1 to the destination text block but left it\nonly there. sourcesDestRow stretches both columns to the taller one, so when a\nmulti-source Select wraps onto several lines the \"Requires advanced setup\" hint\nkept its 32px minimum and stayed at the top of the slot while the arrow centered\nwithin the full row. It now fills the column the same way.\n\nAlso restores the indentation the suggestion dropped on the min-height line and\nrefreshes the comment, which still described the fixed-height behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfa61f4ff2276594487ee0ec1c95aaa3cbcaa1fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/git/trees/bfa61f4ff2276594487ee0ec1c95aaa3cbcaa1fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-importer/git/commits/2f45178858844d8162ea02232d7dd9d03adebe79","verification":{"payload":"tree bfa61f4ff2276594487ee0ec1c95aaa3cbcaa1fc\nparent ea10435049bc1d4bc48134c245514bcf473c52a7\nauthor idaiv <138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com> 1788252516 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788252516 +0200\n\n[Data Importer] Highlight the expanded mapping and align its destination column (#685)\n\n* [Data Importer] Highlight the expanded mapping and align its destination column\n\nHighlights the open mapping section. Collapsed and expanded sections looked\nidentical apart from the chevron, so nothing marked the one being edited. The\nexpanded panel now carries the primary border from the design.\n\nThe rule needs !important. The SDK draws the panel border from\n.ant-collapse.collapse-item--theme-default.collapse-item--bordered, which\noutranks the wrapper selector, and it is a border shorthand rather than a\nborder-color. The drag-and-drop rules alongside it are !important for the same\nreason and are one class more specific, so dragging still takes over the border\nwhile it is in progress.\n\nSwaps the settings gear for the transformation icon on the Advanced button and\non the badge that sits above the arrow when an advanced setup exists, matching\nthe design. The badge was already wired to isAdvanced and only had the wrong\nicon. The icon already ships in the studio-ui-bundle library, so nothing has to\nbe added there. arrowGearIcon is renamed to arrowAdvancedIcon to match what it\nnow renders.\n\nAligns the advanced destination text with the rest of the row. It used\nfontSizeSM, which resolves to 10px against the 12px every control around it\nuses, and it filled only its line box at the top of the slot, so it sat above\nthe vertical center of the source Select and the arrow. It now uses fontSize\nand occupies the same controlHeight box as the Select it replaces, centered\nwithin it. The \"Requires advanced setup\" hint shares that slot and had both\nproblems, so it follows the same rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Center the destination text when the source Select wraps\n\nThe applied suggestion added flex: 1 to the destination text block but left it\nonly there. sourcesDestRow stretches both columns to the taller one, so when a\nmulti-source Select wraps onto several lines the \"Requires advanced setup\" hint\nkept its 32px minimum and stayed at the top of the slot while the arrow centered\nwithin the full row. It now fills the column the same way.\n\nAlso restores the indentation the suggestion dropped on the min-height line and\nrefreshes the comment, which still described the fixed-height behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <no